<Layout title="Receive">
  <h1>Receive offline</h1>
  <p>
    The Go recipient tool is in development; no signed downloadable receiver is
    available yet.
  </p>
  <p>
    The development receiver reads raw ciphertext and a local encrypted private
    PEM, prompts without echo, authenticates the message and saves exact plaintext
    to a new private Windows file. It never asks you to upload private material
    to this website. Use synthetic data until the release gates close.
  </p>
  <pre><code>.\zodiac-decrypt.exe decrypt --key ".\rsa-private-encrypted.pem" --in ".\ciphertext.txt" --out ".\message.txt"</code></pre>
  <p>Choose a new output name in a private, nonsynced folder on a local fixed disk.
    Existing files, network/device paths, drive aliases, streams and reparse
    redirection are rejected. The receiver preserves exact authenticated UTF-8
    bytes and never prints plaintext or opens an editor. Saved files persist.</p>
  <p>Exit codes: 2 for usage/ciphertext format, 3 for key unlock, 4 for message
    authentication, 5 for local filesystem errors and 130 for cancellation.
    A failed authentication creates no output. Whitespace is not stripped from
    the raw file. Other receiver platforms are currently unsupported.</p>
  <p>Before any future release use, verify its publisher, signature and full file
    hash through an independently trusted channel. These checks, release custody
    guidance and integrated independent review are still pending.</p>
</Layout>
